{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1354922-liminal-homebrew","id":1354922,"title":"Liminal Homebrew","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-14T14:17:53-08:00","id":1354922,"title":"Liminal Homebrew","content":"This is kind of a long shot considering the only things we know about them are a two page introduction and a QC entry but has anyone even attempted a homebrewing of the Liminals? Now that the DB and Lunars are out they're the splat i'm most curious about. I love the aesthetic, am a fan of Attribute based exalts and like a more Terrestrial power level","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23840-teal-tara","name":"Teal Tara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T16:08:08-08:00","id":1354936,"title":"","content":"I have started one but, very barebones (About 52 ish Charms) and kinda uninspired I think. Inspiration for it strikes rarely, and they're so different mechanically (since they don't really need to fear death all that much) that you kind of need to go into a wholly different mindset compared to other splats, I feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T16:21:50-08:00","id":1354938,"title":"","content":"Maybe you could look at Mummy and/or Promethean for inspiration? There should be some thematic similarities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T18:28:28-08:00","id":1354951,"title":"","content":"Let's think about what's in the few QC charms.<br /> <br /> Black Soil's Claim: an offensive charm whose damage-over-time effect keys off the target's wound penalty. For undead targets it instead adds dice of Aggravated damage that increase with wound penalty.<br /> <br /> Stitched-Flesh Juggernaut: The QC adds 2 STR, possibly keying off Essence given the QC is E2. It adds 4 with anima up. It can be reset by spending motes and absorbing muscle from a corpse.<br /> <br /> Weeping Crimson Gaze: Doubles up to three 9s on an attack roll, also being able to see and hit dematerialized undead (specifically undead, by the text) for the instant. The character's wound penalty reduces the cost.<br /> <br /> Patchwork Body Reconstruction: After killing a nontrivial living foe or a fleshy undead, heal up to 2 (Essence?) non-Agg HLs or a crippling injury.<br /> <br /> Skeletal Spike Embrace: Extrude bones to get the benefits of cover and also hurt grapple partners or people hitting you up close til next turn; at your -4 HLs, the effect is greater all around.<br /> <br /> Clambering Horror Chase: Enhance a rush, rushing from afar and moving up walls and such. This can be committed for the scene, but it burns out a limb and requires it to be replaced.<br /> <br /> So...<br /> We have stuff playing on your and others' wound penalties, rewarding you for targeting the hurt and giving you discounts or boosts for your injuries. <br /> We have stuff that's specifically keyed for undead.<br /> We interact with corpses.<br /> We can burn out body parts for big effects.<br /> <br /> That, and using the core's stated themes for the aspects, should help a little bit. I'm not sure how to divide up the Attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8026,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","user":"Beans","date":". 12-14-2019, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T05:03:08-08:00","id":1354981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1354922-liminal-homebrew?p=1354951#post1354951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how to divide up the Attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm going to be lazy (and, perhaps, kind of a tool) and quote myself. From <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347462-trying-to-homebrew-liminals-charm-ideas-appreciated\">another thread on the topic</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My personal setup leaves <b>Blood</b> with Charisma (passion, connections) and Wits (purity, but also navigation and guidance), <b>Breath</b> with Dexterity (grace and subtle action) and Perception (understanding and reflection),<b> Flesh</b> with your set of Strength (force, madness, savagery) and Appearance (metamorphosis and lust), <b>Marrow</b> with Manipulation (secrecy) and Intelligence (analysis, obsession), and <b>Soil</b> with Stamina (resilience, resurrection) and Intelligence (mysticism, creation). </div> </div> </div> Intelligence repeats mostly because <i>Masters of Jade</i> pitched Liminals as &quot;sorcerer-exorcists,&quot; and both sorcery and exorcism slot readily into the Intelligence Attribute.<br /> <br /> Of course, I maintain that Liminals should have a set of Universal Charms to fulfill the essential fantasy of <i>undead ghost-hunter</i>, just as Lunars have Universal Charms to support their role as shapeshifters regardless of build. This would include the typical anti-spirit tech, as well as Charms like Ox-Body Technique and other baseline survival effects, while Intelligence and Stamina Charms would build off these for more esoteric or specific powers, such as binding defeated ghosts into servants of clay or meat, or absorbing a mass of corpses to become a giant of bone and sinew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 12-15-2019, 08:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T17:28:49-08:00","id":1355970,"title":"","content":"I found an answer to my own question. Here's a homebrew i found though I don't know who the author is or if it's still actively being worked on. <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12dqVZ9zTLDadz24szTwQvq9HiIjHQ70UpSHVygHQDBE/edit#heading=h.9fprxbj0djgn\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12dqVZ9zTLDadz24szTwQvq9HiIjHQ70UpSHVygHQDBE/edit#heading=h.9fprxbj0djgn\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12dqVZ9zTLDadz24szTwQvq9HiIjHQ70UpSHVygHQDBE/edit#heading=h.9fprxbj0djgn\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/12dqVZ9zTLDadz24szTwQvq9HiIjHQ70UpSHVygHQDBE/edit#heading=h.9fprxbj0djgn </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23840-teal-tara","name":"Teal Tara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}